<description>
Paint teal square blocks at the two outward opposite corners of each diagonal foreground motif.

Input structure
- The canvas has one background color and one foreground color.
- Each 8-connected foreground object has a square bounding box split into a 2-by-2 grid of equal square blocks.
- Exactly two diagonal blocks of that footprint are filled with the foreground color; the other two are background.

Rule
- Preserve the input.
- If the filled blocks are northwest/southeast, paint teal blocks just outside the northeast and southwest corners.
- If the filled blocks are northeast/southwest, paint teal blocks just outside the northwest and southeast corners.
- Clip any painted block at the grid boundary.

Key insight
- The green pixels are scaled square blocks; the task completes the perpendicular diagonal of the expanded block layout.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "transform_in_place",
  "src": "8-connected foreground motifs on a background canvas; each motif is two equal filled square blocks in diagonal corners of a 2x2 block footprint",
  "transform": "preserve the input; paint teal square blocks of the same size in the two outward corners of the opposite diagonal, clipped at the grid boundary"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 10x10 [observed]
  background: BLACK [observed]
  foreground: single color, not TEAL (GREEN in all examples [observed])
  motifs:
    count: 1-2
    structure: each motif is a 2x2 arrangement of equal square blocks; exactly 2 diagonal blocks are filled with FG, other 2 are BG
    block_size: 1-3 (motif bounding box = 2*block_size square)
    diagonal: NW-SE or NE-SW (either orientation per motif)
  placement:
    - motif bounding boxes lie fully within the grid
    - motifs do not overlap each other
    - teal target areas (the opposite-diagonal block positions, possibly clipped at grid boundary) must be BG in the input
    - teal targets must not overlap each other or any motif
  transform:
    - preserve input; for each motif, paint teal (8) square blocks of same block_size at the two outward opposite-diagonal corners
    - NW-SE filled -> teal at NE-outer and SW-outer; NE-SW filled -> teal at NW-outer and SE-outer
    - teal blocks clip at grid boundary (partially visible is OK)

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. choose grid 10x10, BG=BLACK, FG=random color != TEAL
    2. choose num_motifs (1-2), for each pick block_size 1-3 and diagonal orientation
    3. for each motif, compute 4 block positions (2 FG + 2 teal targets); a motif needs 4 block_size squares arranged in a 2x2 plus 2 outer diagonal blocks
    4. place motifs on grid ensuring all 4 positions (2 FG blocks within grid, 2 teal blocks at least partially within grid) are non-overlapping and on BG; reject if collision
    5. build output by filling FG and teal blocks; derive input by removing teal blocks (set to BG)
```
